does GPT Image 2.5 Flare support?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_1taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_1taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">GPT Image 2.5 Flare supports the 1:1, 3:2, 2:3, 4:3, 3:4, 16:9 and 2 more aspect ratios and can generate up to 10 images per request.</p></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="border-b border-border last:border-0"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="flex"><button type="button" data-value="" data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" id="base-ui-_R_2daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" tabindex="0" class="flex flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-medium transition-colors duration-fast ease-smooth-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-focus-border focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-panel-open]&gt;svg.accordion-chevron]:-scale-y-100 gap-4 py-4 text-left text-base hover:text-foreground">What inputs and outputs does GPT Image 2.5 Flare support?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_2daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_2daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">GPT Image 2.5 Flare accepts text and images as input and returns images. Up to 16 reference images can be attached to one request for image editing.</p></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="border-b border-border last:border-0"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="flex"><button type="button" data-value="" data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" id="base-ui-_R_2taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" tabindex="0" class="flex flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-medium transition-colors duration-fast ease-smooth-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-focus-border focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-panel-open]&gt;svg.accordion-chevron]:-scale-y-100 gap-4 py-4 text-left text-base hover:text-foreground">What other image models does OpenAI have?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_2taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_2taepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0"><a href="/openai/gpt-image-2.5-sunburst" class="underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors">GPT Image 2.5 Sunburst</a>, <a href="/openai/gpt-image-2" class="underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors">GPT Image 2</a>, <a href="/openai/gpt-image-1-mini" class="underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors">GPT Image 1 Mini</a> and 1 more are other image models from OpenAI.</p></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="border-b border-border last:border-0"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" class="flex"><button type="button" data-value="" data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" aria-disabled="false" aria-expanded="false" id="base-ui-_R_3daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" tabindex="0" class="flex flex-1 cursor-pointer items-center justify-between font-medium transition-colors duration-fast ease-smooth-out focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-focus-border focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-panel-open]&gt;svg.accordion-chevron]:-scale-y-100 gap-4 py-4 text-left text-base hover:text-foreground">When was GPT Image 2.5 Flare released?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down accordion-chevron size-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground transition-transform duration-fast ease-smooth-out motion-reduce:transition-none [&amp;_path]:[vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke]" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-orientation="vertical" data-index="-1" data-closed="" hidden="" id="base-ui-_R_3daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH1_" aria-labelledby="base-ui-_R_3daepbqubsnqbt3dml9ivbH2_" role="region" style="--accordion-panel-height:auto;--accordion-panel-width:auto" data-testid="faq-panel" class="h-(--accordion-panel-height) overflow-hidden transition-[height,opacity] duration-slow ease-smooth-out data-[starting-style]:h-0 data-[starting-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:h-0 data-[ending-style]:opacity-0 data-[ending-style]:duration-medium motion-reduce:transition-opacity motion-reduce:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:duration-quick motion-reduce:data-[starting-style]:h-auto motion-reduce:data-[ending-style]:h-auto text-body leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&amp;&gt;div]:pb-4"><div class="pb-3 pt-0"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">GPT Image 2.5 Flare was released on September 9, 2026.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is GPT Image 2.5 Flare?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GPT Image 2.5 Flare is an image generation and editing model from OpenAI, positioned as the speed-oriented tier of the GPT Image 2.5 series. It is suited to high-volume everyday generation, creator content, and rapid prototyping via the dedicated Images API."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does GPT Image 2.5 Flare cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GPT Image 2.5 Flare costs $8.00/M input tokens and $8.00/M output tokens, with separate rates for Cache Read at $2.00/M tokens, Text Input at $5.00/M tokens, and Image Output at $30.00/M tokens."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What image aspect ratios does GPT Image 2.5 Flare support?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GPT Image 2.5 Flare supports the 1:1, 3:2, 2:3, 4:3, 3:4, 16:9 and 2 more aspect ratios and can generate up to 10 images per request."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What inputs and outputs does GPT Image 2.5 Flare support?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GPT Image 2.5 Flare accepts text and images as input and returns images. Up to 16 reference images can be attached to one request for image editing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What other image models does OpenAI have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GPT Image 2.5 Sunburst, GPT Image 2, GPT Image 1 Mini and 1 more are other image models from OpenAI."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When was GPT Image 2.5 Flare released?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GPT Image 2.5 Flare was released on September 9, 2026."}}]}</script></div><script>$RC("B:9","S:9")</script><div hidden id="S:a"><div class="my-8 w-full first:mt-0"><div class="min-w-0 w-full"><h2>More models from<!-- --> <span class=""><a class="text-inherit underline" href="/openai">OpenAI</a></span></h2><div class="mt-4"><div class="overflow-hidden"><section class="group/carousel hover:cursor-move relative w-full" aria-roledescription="carousel"><div><div class="flex -ml-4"><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/openai/gpt-6.1-sol-pro"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">GPT-6.1 Sol Pro</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">GPT-6.1 Sol Pro is the same underlying model as <span>GPT-6.1 Sol</span>, served with <code class="rounded-md bg-card-hover px-1.5 text-foreground">reasoning.mode</code> set to <code class="rounded-md bg-card-hover px-1.5 text-foreground">pro</code> for higher-quality responses on complex tasks.</p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0"><strong>Cost note:</strong> pro mode spends far more reasoning tokens per request, so a typical request costs several times more than the same request on GPT-6.1 Sol and takes much longer to complete. It is intended for hard, high-stakes problems where the extra accuracy justifies the cost. For everyday coding, agentic, and chat workloads, use <span>GPT-6.1 Sol</span> instead.</p>
<p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">Learn more in OpenAI&#x27;s docs: <span>https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/reasoning#reasoning-mode</span></p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>1.1M context</span></span><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block size-[0.215em] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-current align-middle"></span><span>$2 / $10</span></span></div></a></div><div role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" class="min-w-0 shrink-0 grow-0 pl-4 basis-auto"><a class="group flex h-full w-64 shrink-0 flex-col justify-between gap-y-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-left md:w-80" href="/openai/gpt-6.1-sol"><div class="line-clamp-1 text-heading font-semibold text-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground group-hover:underline">GPT-6.1 Sol</div><div class="line-clamp-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><p class="mb-3 whitespace-pre-wrap break-words leading-6 last:mb-0">GPT-6.1 Sol is an upgrade to GPT-6 Sol from OpenAI, positioned below the flagship GPT-6 Astra in the GPT-6 series. It is suited for agentic coding, computer use, document-heavy professional work, and multi-step business workflow automation, and approaches Astra-level results on these tasks at a much lower cost. Compared with GPT-6 Sol, it makes fewer factual errors and is more reliable at respecting explicit restrictions and user intent during agentic tasks.</p></div><div aria-label="Model details" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-overline text-muted-foreground tabular-nums"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span>Text</span></span><span class="inline-flex